{"result": {"id": "27c85656-1bf1-42c1-b739-79901eb19a6a", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "{\n    \"title\": \"ABAP Environment 2508 Overview\",\n    \"summary\": \"This report provides an overview of the key features and updates in ABAP Environment 2508, highlighting the importance of these changes in the context of the ABAP ecosystem.\",\n    \"rating\": 8.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The high importance rating reflects the critical role that ABAP Environment 2508 plays in supporting the development and deployment of SAP applications, with a focus on improved performance, security, and user experience.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Direct Push-Based Integration\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Direct Push-Based Integration feature in ABAP Environment 2508 enables the connection of neighboring ABAP systems, allowing for the exchange of data and business events between them. This feature is crucial for maintaining data consistency and ensuring seamless communication between systems. [Data: Sources (164), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 16), (2024, 08, 16))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Display IAM Apps\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Display IAM Apps feature in ABAP Environment 2508 provides a comprehensive overview of assigned business roles, including external apps and related authorizations. This feature is essential for ensuring that users have the necessary permissions to access and manage SAP applications. [Data: Sources (162), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 09), (2024, 08, 16))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Exposing APIs via UCL\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Exposing APIs via UCL feature in ABAP Environment 2508 enables the creation of packages and assignment of APIs to ABAP development tools for Eclipse. This feature is critical for exposing APIs to external systems and ensuring seamless integration with other applications. [Data: Sources (163), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 09), (2024, 08, 16))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Improved CDS Buffering - Buffer Propagation\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Improved CDS Buffering - Buffer Propagation feature in ABAP Environment 2508 optimizes memory consumption and enables the ASQL runtime to read denormalized elements within CDS view entities directly from the ABAP buffer. This feature is essential for improving performance and reducing memory usage. [Data: Sources (164), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 16), (2024, 08, 16))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Maintain Business Roles\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Maintain Business Roles feature in ABAP Environment 2508 enables the mass change of business roles, including derived business roles. This feature is critical for ensuring that users have the necessary permissions to access and manage SAP applications. [Data: Sources (165), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 09), (2024, 08, 16))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"OData API: Support User - Read Integration\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The OData API: Support User - Read Integration feature in ABAP Environment 2508 enables the retrieval of support user data, including related authorizations and authorization objects. This feature is essential for ensuring that users have the necessary permissions to access and manage SAP applications. [Data: Sources (166), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 09), (2024, 08, 16))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"OData APIs for Communication Management\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The OData APIs for Communication Management feature in ABAP Environment 2508 enables the creation of APIs for communication management data, including communication arrangements, systems, and users. This feature is critical for ensuring seamless communication between systems and users. [Data: Sources (167), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 09), (2024, 08, 16))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Outbound Emails\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Outbound Emails feature in ABAP Environment 2508 enables the monitoring of asynchronous email status and the sending of emails asynchronously. This feature is essential for ensuring that emails are delivered successfully and that users have the necessary permissions to access and manage SAP applications. [Data: Sources (168), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 16), (2024, 08, 16))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Outbound SQL Using CDS External Entities\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Outbound SQL Using CDS External Entities feature in ABAP Environment 2508 enables the access of external databases using ABAP CDS and ABAP SQL. This feature is critical for ensuring seamless integration with other applications and databases. [Data: Sources (169), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 16), (2024, 08, 16))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Improved CDS Buffering - Buffer Delegation\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Improved CDS Buffering - Buffer Delegation feature in ABAP Environment 2505 optimizes ABAP memory consumption for scenarios using CDS Entity Buffering. This feature is essential for improving performance and reducing memory usage. [Data: Sources (851), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 16), (2025, 05, 16))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Include Start Authorizations for Custom Services in Provider Support Role\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Include Start Authorizations for Custom Services in Provider Support Role feature in ABAP Environment 2505 enables the inclusion of start authorizations for custom services in provider support roles. This feature is critical for ensuring that users have the necessary permissions to access and manage SAP applications. [Data: Sources (852), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 11), (2025, 05, 16))]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"date_range\": [\"2024-08-16\", \"2025-05-16\"]\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null}}], "created": 1758943046, "model": "gpt-4o", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1274, "prompt_tokens": 6266, "total_tokens": 7540, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": null, "outputTps": 51.257292295312816, "duration": 24.855}}, "input": {"messages": [{"content": "\nYou are an AI assistant that helps a human analyst to perform general information discovery.\nInformation discovery is the process of identifying and assessing relevant information associated with certain entities (e.g., organizations and individuals) within a network.\n\n# Goal\nWrite a comprehensive report of a community, given a list of entities that belong to the community as well as their relationships and optional associated claims.\nThe report will be used to inform decision-makers about information associated with the community and their potential impact.\nThe content of this report includes an overview of the community's key entities, their core attributes or capabilities, their connections, and noteworthy claims.\nRetain as much time specific information as possible so your end user can build a timeline of events.\n\n# Report Structure\nThe report should include the following sections:\n- TITLE: community's name that represents its key entities - title should be short but specific. When possible, include representative named entities in the title. Avoid including phrases like 'eligibility assessment' or 'eligibility assessment report' in the title.\n- SUMMARY: An executive summary of the community's overall structure, how its entities are related to each other, and significant program-specific or eligibility-related insights.\n- IMPORTANCE RATING: A float score between 0-10 that represents the importance of entities within the community..\n- RATING EXPLANATION: Give a single sentence explanation of the importance rating.\n- DETAILED FINDINGS: A list of 5-10 key insights about the community. Each insight should have a short summary followed by multiple paragraphs of explanatory text grounded according to the grounding rules below. Be comprehensive.\n- DATE RANGE: A range of dates (YYYY-MM-DD) with the format [START, END] which corresponds to the date range of text units and intermediate reports used to build the report.\n\nReturn output as a well-formed JSON-formatted string with the following format. Don't use any unnecessary escape sequences. The output should be a single JSON object that can be parsed by json.loads.\n    {\n        \"title\": \"<report_title>\",\n        \"summary\": \"<executive_summary>\",\n        \"rating\": <importance_rating>,\n        \"rating_explanation\": \"<rating_explanation>\",\n        \"findings\": [{\"summary\":\"<insight_1_summary>\", \"explanation\": \"<insight_1_explanation\"}, {\"summary\":\"<insight_2_summary>\", \"explanation\": \"<insight_2_explanation\"}],\n\t\t\"date_range\": [\"<date range start>\", \"<date range end>\"],\n\n    }\n\n# Grounding Rules\nPoints supported by data should list their data references as follows:\n\n\"This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: <dataset name> (record ids), <dataset name> (record ids)].\"\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n\"Person X resolved a major issue with project Y [Data: Sources (1, 5),  Date_Range ((2001, 05, 12), (2001, 05, 14))]. He also made major updates to the database of app Y [Data: Reports (2, 4), Sources (7, 23, 2, 34, 46, +more), Date_Range ((2001, 05, 15), (2001, 05, 18))\"\"\n\nwhere 1, 2, 4, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, and 46 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nLimit the total report length to 2000 words.\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nSOURCES\nid, text\n1, Text: From: compliance.office@enron.com To: management.team@enron.com Cc: legal.team@enron.com, risk@enron.com Date: Wed, 12 Jul 2000 08:30:00 -0600 (CST) Subject: Quick Update on Compliance & Risk Efforts\n2, Quick update on what's been cooking in Compliance and Risk Management. Risk Management is stepping up — They've been tightening up on our financial risk assessments and mitigation strategies since early this year.\n3, Their efforts are key to keeping us on solid ground financially and in compliance with the latest market regulations as of mid-2000. It's crucial for our strategic planning and helps us stay ahead.\n5, Legal's keeping us in check — The Legal Compliance team is on top of ensuring all our operations are up to scratch with legal standards. They're especially focused on improving our corporate governance and contract management as of the second quarter of 2000. This is critical for keeping our operations smooth and legally sound.\n9, Working together — Risk Management and Legal Compliance have been syncing up better than ever since the start of Q2 2000. They're making sure our strategies are not just effective but also fully compliant. This coordination is essential for our integrated governance approach.\n10, Your thoughts? — How do these updates impact your area? Got ideas on how we can do better? Give your department heads a shout.\n11, Thanks for staying engaged. Let's keep pushing for better and smarter ways to work. Cheers, Jane Doe\n\nOutput:\n\n{\n    \"title\": \"Enron Compliance and Risk Management Overview as of July 2000\",\n    \"summary\": \"This report delves into Enron's key departments focusing on compliance and risk management, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2000.\",\n    \"rating\": 9.2,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The high importance rating reflects the critical roles that the Risk Management and Legal Compliance Departments play in ensuring Enron's adherence to financial and legal regulations, crucial for maintaining the company's integrity and operational stability.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Risk Management Operational Scope\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Risk Management Department at Enron plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2000, helps safeguard Enron against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes.\n\n[Data: Sources (2, 3), Date_Range ((2000, 01, 01), (2000, 07, 12))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Legal Compliance and Governance\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Legal Compliance Department ensures that all Enron's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and contract management, noted starting Q2 2000, is crucial in maintaining Enron's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices.\n\n[Data: Source (5), Date_Range ((2000, 04, 01), (2000, 07, 12))]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Collaboration between the Risk Management and Legal Compliance Departments, established in Q2 2000, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at Enron. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements.\n\n[Data: Sources (9), Date_Range ((2000, 04, 01), (2000, 07, 12))]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"date_range\": [\"2000-01-01\", \"2000-07-12\"]\n}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----SOURCES-----\nid,text,entity_degree\n164,\"--- Record 2441 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Direct Push-Based Integration\nDescription: With direct push-based integration, you can connect neighboring ABAP Systems with each other. In this scenario, the connected systems exchange data (like business events) by calling each other directly via RFC.  See Direct Push-Based Integration.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2442 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Display IAM Apps\nDescription: With this feature you can display IAM apps of all supported types. This helps you to keep an overview of the assigned business roles. For external apps, you can view the related authorizations including authorization objects, authorization instances and authorization fields.  For more information, see Display IAM Apps.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-09\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2443 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Exposing APIs via UCL\nDescription: You can now expose APIs via UCL (Unified Customer Landscape) for the usage in BAS (SAP Business Application Studio) and SAP Build. You can do this by creating packages and assigning them to the required APIs in ABAP development tools for Eclipse.  For more information, see Working with API Packages.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-09\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2444 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Improved CDS Buffering - Buffer Propagation\nDescription: Extend the reach of the CDS/ABAP buffering approach and optimize the memory consumption with buffer propagation to enable the ASQL runtime to read denormalized elements within CDS view entities directly from the ABAP buffer instead of pushing the joins to the database.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2445 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Maintain Business Roles\nDescription: The Mass Change Wizard has been expanded so that you can also use it for derived business roles.  For more information, see Maintain Business Roles.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-09\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2446 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: OData API: Support User - Read Integration\nDescription: The following API is now available to retrieve support user data:  Support User – Read Integration  The following corresponding communication scenario is available:  Support User Request Log Integration (SAP_COM_0347)   For more information, see Support User - Read Integration.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-09\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2447 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: OData APIs for Communication Management\nDescription: The following APIs are now available for Communication Management data:      Communication Arrangement - Read and Write Integration      Communication System - Read and Write Integration      Communication User - Read and Write Integration      The following corresponding communication scenario is available:    Communication Management Integration scenario (SAP_COM_0A48)      For more information, see Integrating Communication Management Data (Read and Write)\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-09\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2448 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Outbound Emails\nDescription: This feature enables you to monitor the status of asynchronous emails using the interface IF_BCS_MAIL_STATUS_MONITOR. The released API CL_BCS_MAIL_MESSAGE that is used for sending emails provides the option to send emails asynchronously. To monitor the status of the emails a released API is required.  For more information, see   .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2449 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Outbound SQL Using CDS External Entities\nDescription: With ABAP SQL as outbound service type, you can now access external databases using ABAP CDS and ABAP SQL. This feature is integrated into ABAP Cloud concepts, including CDS modeling of the external data sources, and natively uses SAP HANA federation capabilities (taking advantage of SAP HANA Smart Data Access). In this new dynamic access, you can model external data sources using the new CDS external entities and the new logical external schemas. The CDS external entities can\",691\n91,\"--- Record 851 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Improved CDS Buffering - Buffer Delegation\nDescription: Optimize the ABAP memory consumption for scenarios which make use of CDS Entity Buffering:  Provide support for \"\"delegated buffers\"\" to allow buffering on CDS view entity-level by reusing the buffer on table-level at runtime.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 852 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Include Start Authorizations for Custom Services in Provider Support Role\nDescription: Provider support roles now contain start authorizations for custom services that are shipped as part of an add-on.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-11\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 853 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Including Custom Authorizations in Development Test Role\nDescription: The business catalog SAP_CORE_BC_EXT_TST for development test roles is now continuously extended, not only with the start authorizations for custom services, but also with full authorizations for any custom authorization object included in the authorization default values. This improves testability during the early development stages by enabling the developer to test services from a functional perspective without asking the administrator to assign roles with missing authorizations.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-27\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 854 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Increased SAP HANA Cloud Backup Retention Time to 30 Days\nDescription: Backups of the SAP HANA Cloud database of an SAP BTP ABAP environment system are now kept for 30 days instead of 14 days.  For more information, see Backups.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-27\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 855 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Message Monitoring for Integration Experts\nDescription: You can now download the original payload of your message. While in Message Monitoring for Integration Experts, open the message, go to Data Content  Data Structure and choose Download Original Payload.  See Message Monitoring for Integration Experts.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-11\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 856 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: New Email Configuration for the Upload Business Configuration App\nDescription: There is a new configuration available for the app Upload Business Configuration. You can now use the following entities:     SMAIL_VM_DF_ADDR      SMAIL_VM_RCV_DOM      SMAIL_VM_SND_DOM      For more information, see Upload Business Configuration.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-18\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 857 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: New Skip Function within the Application Job Templates App\nDescription: You can now skip a single execution of a periodic job chain in the Application Job Templates app.  See Creating an Application Job Template.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 858 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Null Value Handling\nDescription: You can now find an overview of the differences in the behavior of null values and initial values in OData V2 and V4 with regard to sorting and filtering on the Fiori Elements UI as well as explicit filtering through OData Web API request. See: Null Value Handling  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 859 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: OData UI Service from Scratch\nDescription: You can create all RAP-service related repository objects from scratch by using the OData UI Service from Scratch wizard. See: OData UI Service from Scratch\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 860 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Referenced SAPUI5 Version\nDescription: As part of hotfix collection 3 (which is used for the standard upgrade), SAPUI5 version 1.133.2 is used for the administrator’s SAP Fiori launchpad, SAP-delivered Fior\",202\n684,\"--- Record 3341 ---\nComponent: Data Attribute Recommendation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Resuse of Dataset Schemas\nDescription: We’ve fixed an issue related to the resuse of dataset schemas.  You can now reuse the same dataset schema with different datasets.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-06\nValid as Of: 2024-03-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3342 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Download client logs related to crash reports\nDescription: (Version 2402) When a crash occurs, you can now download any available client log files that are related to the crash report, to help analyze the crash. Previously, the related client logs were not made available to download, so you needed to search for the data manually.  See     Viewing Crash Group Analytics      Configuring Mobile Client Log Upload    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-27\nValid as Of: 2024-03-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3343 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: API Artifact\nDescription: You can now create an OData API artifact using a .edmx file. This functionality enables users to easily generate and manage OData APIs by leveraging existing .edmx files.   See: Create an API Artifact Using URL\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-05\nValid as Of: 2024-03-05\nVersion: 2313\n\n--- Record 3344 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Edge Integration Cell: 8.13.*      Increment: 2313    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-05\nValid as Of: 2024-03-05\nVersion: 2313\n\n--- Record 3345 ---\nComponent: Graph\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Manage Business Data Graphs using Graph Configuration API\nDescription: The Graph Configuration API simplifies the process of managing your business data graphs automatically. Whether you need to create, update, or delete business data graphs, this API provides an automated option to achieve these tasks.  The primary focus is to enable a seamless integration of business data graph management with your existing CI/CD pipelines.  For more information, see:     Configure Entitlement for Graph      Manage Business Data Graphs using Graph Configuration API    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-05\nValid as Of: 2024-03-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3346 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: Update to version 2.2.0\nDescription: Version 2.2.0 of the API Gateway module brings the following changes:    We've introduced PodDisruptionBudget for Ory Oathkeeper. For more information, see the PR.      We've extended APIRule access strategies with no_auth to restrict accessible methods, thereby minimizing the exposure of the API.      Now, the Kyma modules use consistent labeling. To learn more about the labels that the API Gateway module uses, see Labeling Resources.      The API Gateway custom resources (CR) use the Warning state instead of Error when there is more than one APIGateway CR on the cluster. For more information, see the PR.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-20\nValid as Of: 2024-03-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3347 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Apps\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Mobile\nDescription:   Enabled SAP Mobile Services  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-05\nValid as Of: 2024-03-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3348 ---\nComponent: SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Integration with new credit agency: Informa D&B Spain\nDescription: The credit agency Informa D&B Spain is now connected to SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for credit integration.  More information:  Available Credit Agency Products and Features  Your Tasks for Integrating a New Credit Agency\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-05\nValid as Of: 2024-03-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3349 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Istio and API Gateway modules: temporary downtime in the fast channel\nDescription: We plan to eliminate technical debt in the Istio and API Gateway modules on the default Kyma domain in the fast channel. This will take place outside of the maintenance window and might result in a temporary downtime lasting several minutes.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-04\nValid as Of: 2024-03-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3350 ---\nComponent: Kyma\",177\n\n\nOutput:\n", "role": "user"}], "parameters": {"model": "gpt-4o", "frequency_penalty": 0.0, "max_tokens": null, "n": 1, "presence_penalty": 0.0, "temperature": 0.0, "top_p": 1.0, "response_format": {"type": "json_object"}}}, "key": "chat_create_community_report_ea056298a418662539f514c1d54398aa04efdcaff1e888bcde5de2373817da49_v2"}